94-107, 148-179, 181-203, 252-267), p.pools currently holds both []byte and
*Buffer which can cause a panic when Get/Put and GetBuffer/PutBuffer mix types;
add a new field bufPools sync.Map for *sync.Pool of *Buffer, update the struct
to have separate maps (p.pools for []byte pools and p.bufPools for *Buffer
pools), implement a helper getBufferPool(size int) *sync.Pool that loads or
stores a pool in p.bufPools (New can be nil or create *Buffer as needed), change
GetBuffer/PutBuffer to use p.getBufferPool(size) instead of p.getPool(size), and
stop pre-creating *Buffer pools in initializePools (only pre-create []byte
pools); ensure all type assertions use the correct pool map to avoid
heterogeneous-type panics.
```

